{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And by your sword you shall live.</b> In reward for taking your gear and bow in My commandments." "<b>[And by your sword.</b> By your sword you shall live.]" "<b>And your brother you shall serve.</b> Esav said: since he has set a master over me, he will treat me with contempt. His father said to him: <b>and by your sword you shall live</b> — your service will be with the sword, and that is not a contemptuous treatment. Esav said: even so, with sword-service he will burden me too much. He said to him: <b>and your brother you shall serve</b> — in this service, and he will have compassion on you." "<b>When you grow restive.</b> Like ״אָרִיד בְּשִׂיחִי״ — when he makes his yoke heavy upon you too much, <b>and you shall break his yoke</b> — you abandon his land and do not serve him, like what soldiers do when the officer burdens them too much: they abandon the land they hold from him and no longer serve him. Another interpretation: <b>when you grow restive</b> — from the root וירד (to go down) from Yaakov, meaning when you rule. <b>And you shall break his yoke</b> — and so we find in his days: Edom rebelled and set a king over themselves."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:24.584663942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}